.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments-charge - Charge a payment — authorize + capture in one call (no escrow)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments charge  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Prepare the transaction that calls charge() on the RAIL0 contract.
Combines authorize + capture into a single on-chain call; funds move
directly from payer to payee without an escrow window.

.PP
The payment must have been created with -C/--charge and signed by the
payer via 'payments create -p' (create + sign in one atomic step).
The API returns 202 immediately: broadcasting is not settling. The payment
stays at "signed" until rail0-indexer sees the on-chain event and the API
transitions it to "charged".

.PP
Add -w/--wait to block until that happens (or the operation fails) and exit
non-zero if it didn't land, instead of polling 'payments get \&'.

.PP
Pass --private-key (-p): the CLI signs locally and broadcasts in one step.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for charge

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	Make a re-run safe: the same key returns the first transaction instead of opening a second

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--private-key\fP=""
	Caller's secp256k1 private key (0x-prefixed hex); signs and broadcasts in one step

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=15m0s
	Max time to wait when --wait is set; unset, 10× the chain's measured p90 settlement, kept within 5m–15m

.PP
\fB-w\fP, \fB--wait\fP[=false]
	Block until the operation confirms on-chain (or fails)

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip the confirmation prompt (required to run non-interactively)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payments charge 0xrail0Id… -p @merchant-key --wait
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payments(1)\fP
